      "id": "72b74717",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Agenda: Agentic Workflow (AutoGen)\n",
        "\n",
        "**Overview**\n",
        "Build a simple multi-agent workflow using AutoGen with two collaborating agents.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Agents**\n",
        "- **Researcher** – gathers facts and details  \n",
        "- **Reporting Analyst (Reporter)** – produces a professional report"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "7591492b",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#### AutoGen\n",
        "\n",
        "Created by Microsoft in 2023.  \n",
        "Open-source framework for multi-agent AI systems where LLM-powered agents collaborate, communicate, and use tools to complete tasks.\n",
        "\n",
        "Documentation: https://microsoft.github.io/autogen/stable/  \n",
        "GitHub: https://github.com/microsoft/autogen\n",
        "\n",
        "### Use cases\n",
        "- Multi-agent workflow orchestration  \n",
        "- tool/API integration  "
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 46,
      "id": "c44be51d",
      "metadata": {},
      
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "!pip install -q -U autogen-agentchat autogen-ext[openai] python-dotenv"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "f0ffe90c",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "##### Packages Overview\n",
        "\n",
        "**autogen-agentchat**  \n",
        "For creating and orchestrating agents  \n",
        "Class: `AssistantAgent`  \n",
        "Docs: https://microsoft.github.io/autogen/stable/user-guide/agentchat-user-guide/\n",
        "\n",
        "**autogen-ext**  \n",
        "Integrations with models and tools  \n",
        "Class: `OpenAIChatCompletionClient`  \n",
        "Docs: https://microsoft.github.io/autogen/stable/user-guide/agentchat-user-guide/tutorial/models.html\n",
        "\n",
        "**python-dotenv**  \n",
        "Loads `.env` variables for secure config (e.g., API keys).  \n",
        "Key: `load_dotenv`"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "5ada8d27",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Import Classes and Functions"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 47,
      "id": "d37ea230",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "from autogen_agentchat.agents import AssistantAgent\n",
        "from IPython.display import Markdown, display\n",
        "from autogen_ext.models.openai import OpenAIChatCompletionClient\n",
        "from dotenv import load_dotenv\n",
        "import os"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "adbc8105",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Load API Keys"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 48,
      "id": "20e21511",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "OpenAI API key loaded: True\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "load_dotenv()\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"OpenAI API key loaded:\", os.getenv(\"OPENAI_API_KEY\") is not None)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 49,
      "id": "2a905d07",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "topic = \"ancient egypt\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "4dd8c0a0",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "open_ai_llm_client = OpenAIChatCompletionClient(\n",
        "    model=\"gpt-4o-mini\"\n",
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "df4f7711",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "researcher = AssistantAgent(\n",
        "    name=\"researcher\",\n",
        "    model_client=open_ai_llm_client,\n",
        "    system_message=f\"\"\"You are a skilled and resourceful researcher. Your job is to deeply investigate any assigned topic, intelligently leverage your knowledge and available tools, and synthesize relevant, credible information from trustworthy sources. Your research should emphasize both recent developments and core facts, highlight significance and context, and clearly cite your sources when possible. Focus on accuracy, clarity, and actionable insight in your findings.\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "80f473b0",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "reporting_analyst = AssistantAgent(\n",
        "    name=\"reporting_analyst\",\n",
        "    model_client=open_ai_llm_client,\n",
        "    system_message=f\"\"\"You are a meticulous analyst renowned for your keen attention to detail. You excel at transforming complex information into clear, concise, and actionable reports, making even the most intricate data accessible and understandable for your audience.\"\"\"\n",
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 50,
      "id": "be3a12fa",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "researcher_response = await researcher.run(\n",
        "    task=f\"\"\"\n",
        "      Research the topic: {topic}. \n",
        "      Find interesting facts, people, dates, events, sources, etc...\n",
        "      Output 8-10 detailed bullets about your findings.\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "research = researcher_response.messages[-1].content"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 51,
      "id": "7a357942",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [
        {
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": [
              "Here are 8-10 detailed findings about Ancient Egypt, highlighting interesting facts, key figures, important dates, events, and reliable sources:\n",
              "\n",
              "1. **Timeline of Civilization**: Ancient Egypt's history is often divided into three main kingdoms: the Old Kingdom (circa 2686-2181 BCE), known for the construction of the pyramids; the Middle Kingdom (circa 2055-1650 BCE), which emphasized literature and art; and the New Kingdom (circa 1550-1070 BCE), marked by military expansion and monumental architecture. The civilization began around 3100 BCE with the unification of Upper and Lower Egypt by King Narmer (Menes).\n",
              "\n",
              "2. **Pharaohs and Their Divine Status**: Pharaohs were considered living gods on earth, central to both governance and religious life. Notable pharaohs include Ramses II, who reigned for 66 years and is celebrated for extensive military campaigns and grand monuments like the temples at Abu Simbel; and Tutankhamun, whose nearly intact tomb was discovered in 1922 and has provided significant insights into burial practices and material culture.\n",
              "\n",
              "3. **Pyramid Construction**: The Great Pyramid of Giza, built for Pharaoh Khufu around 2580-2560 BCE, remains an engineering marvel. Originally standing at 146.6 meters (481 feet), it was constructed using approximately 2.3 million blocks of stone, showcasing advanced knowledge in mathematics, architecture, and labor organization. The pyramids served as elaborate tombs, reflecting the Egyptians' beliefs in the afterlife.\n",
              "\n",
              "4. **Hieroglyphic Writing**: Ancient Egyptian writing, known as hieroglyphs, originated around 3200 BCE and consisted of over 700 symbols used for various purposes, including religious texts, administrative records, and monumental inscriptions. The Rosetta Stone, discovered in 1799, was key in deciphering hieroglyphs, leading to significant advancements in understanding Ancient Egyptian language and culture.\n",
              "\n",
              "5. **Religious Practices**: The ancient Egyptians practiced polytheism, worshipping a multitude of gods and goddesses associated with natural events and aspects of life, such as Ra (the sun god), Osiris (god of the afterlife), and Isis (goddess of fertility). Temples were built for worship and to honor the deities, with the most famous being the Temple of Karnak, dedicated to Amun-Ra.\n",
              "\n",
              "6. **Mummification and Afterlife Beliefs**: Mummification, a practice essential for preserving bodies for the afterlife, involved removal of internal organs and treatment with natron salts. The Egyptians believed in an afterlife where the deceased would face judgment by Osiris. The \"Book of the Dead,\" a collection of spells and incantations, was used to guide souls through the afterlife, illustrating the culture's focus on immortality.\n",
              "\n",
              "7. **Social Hierarchy**: Ancient Egyptian society was structured hierarchically. At the top were the pharaoh and nobility, followed by priests and scribes. Farmers and laborers made up the majority of the population, essential for agriculture along the Nile River. Social mobility was limited, although scribes could elevate their status through education and literacy.\n",
              "\n",
              "8. **Noteworthy Women Rulers**: Hatshepsut, a prominent female Pharaoh who ruled during the New Kingdom (circa 1479-1458 BCE), is famed for her successful reign marked by trade expansion and monumental architecture, including her mortuary temple at Deir el-Bahari. She often depicted herself as a male pharaoh to assert authority, emphasizing her unique position in a male-dominated society.\n",
              "\n",
              "9. **Contributions to Mathematics and Medicine**: Ancient Egyptians made significant strides in mathematics and medicine. They developed a decimal system for arithmetic and practical geometry for land surveying, especially after the Nile's annual flooding. Medical texts, such as the Edwin Smith Papyrus, provide insight into surgical practices and the understanding of anatomy and treatments for various ailments.\n",
              "\n",
              "10. **End of the Civilization**: Ancient Egypt eventually fell under foreign rule, beginning with the conquests of Persia (525 BCE), followed by Alexander the Great's campaign in 332 BCE, leading to the establishment of the Ptolemaic Kingdom, which fused Greek and Egyptian cultures. The last ruler, Cleopatra VII (reigned 51-30 BCE), became famous for her political acumen and alliances, ultimately leading to Egypt's annexation by Rome after her defeat by Octavian.\n",
              "\n",
              "### Sources:\n",
              "- \"The Oxford History of Ancient Egypt\" by Ian Shaw\n",
              "- \"The Complete Gods and Goddesses of Ancient Egypt\" by Richard H. Wilkinson\n",
              "- \"Temples, Tombs, and Hieroglyphs: A Popular History of Ancient Egypt\" by Barbara Watterson\n",
              "- Various academic journals and articles on Egyptology."
            ],
            "text/plain": [
              "<IPython.core.display.Markdown object>"
            ]
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "output_type": "display_data"
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "display(Markdown(research))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 52,
      "id": "8ca988c4",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "reporting_analyst_response = await reporting_analyst.run(\n",
        "        task=f\"\"\"\n",
        "          You are provided with the following research notes:\n",
        "          {research}\n",
        "\n",
        "          For each bullet point, expand it into a clear and comprehensive report section.\n",
        "          Retain factual accuracy from the original notes and preserve any attributions to sources. Where appropriate, enrich each section with relevant supporting details or new context that enhances the findings. If any details in the notes appear to be inaccurate, correct them before including them in the final report.\n",
        "\n",
        "          Your output should be a full report structured by main topics, with each topic developed into a distinct section.\n",
        "          At the end, include a concise \"Sources\" list summarizing the cited references.\n",
        "          Format the output as Markdown (but omit enclosing triple backticks).\n",
        "     \n",
        "        \"\"\"\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "report = reporting_analyst_response.messages[-1].content"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 53,
      "id": "26e90a3a",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [
        {
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": [
              "# Comprehensive Report on Ancient Egypt\n",
              "\n",
              "## 1. Timeline of Civilization\n",
              "Ancient Egypt's history is often categorized into three principal kingdoms: the Old Kingdom (circa 2686-2181 BCE), the Middle Kingdom (circa 2055-1650 BCE), and the New Kingdom (circa 1550-1070 BCE). Each of these periods is notable for its distinct contributions to culture, governance, and artistic achievements. The Old Kingdom is renowned for the construction of the iconic pyramids, particularly in Giza, reflecting advanced engineering skills and an organized labor force. The Middle Kingdom emphasized cultural production, notably in literature and the arts, leading to an artistic renaissance. The New Kingdom marked a period of territorial expansion and monumental architecture, exemplified by the grand temples and the extensive building projects initiated by powerful pharaohs. The civilization's origins trace back to around 3100 BCE when King Narmer (Menes) unified Upper and Lower Egypt, establishing a centralized rule that laid the foundation for one of history's most enduring civilizations.\n",
              "\n",
              "## 2. Pharaohs and Their Divine Status\n",
              "Pharaohs in Ancient Egypt were revered as living gods and played a central role in both governance and religion. Their divine status was integral to their authority and legitimacy. Notable pharaohs include Ramses II, who reigned for an impressive 66 years (1279-1213 BCE). He is celebrated for his military campaigns, extensive building projects, and the construction of monumental architecture, including the temples at Abu Simbel, which boast remarkable artistry and grandeur. Another famous figure is Tutankhamun, whose nearly intact tomb was discovered in 1922, revealing a wealth of artifacts that provide profound insights into burial practices and daily life in Ancient Egypt. These historical figures underscore the intertwining of political power and religious beliefs within Egyptian society.\n",
              "\n",
              "## 3. Pyramid Construction\n",
              "The Great Pyramid of Giza, constructed for Pharaoh Khufu around 2580-2560 BCE, is recognized as one of the most extraordinary engineering feats of the ancient world. Initially standing at 146.6 meters (481 feet), it was built from approximately 2.3 million blocks of stone, reflecting the Egyptians' sophisticated understanding of mathematics, architecture, and labor management. The pyramid complex includes not only the main pyramid but also the Great Sphinx, which features a lion's body and a pharaoh's head, believed to represent Khafre, the son of Khufu. The pyramids served as elaborate tombs, embedding the Egyptians’ beliefs regarding the afterlife into their architectural design. The construction of these monumental structures represents a significant chapter in the history of human engineering and reflects the cultural importance placed on death and immortality.\n",
              "\n",
              "## 4. Hieroglyphic Writing\n",
              "Hieroglyphs, the writing system of Ancient Egypt, originated around 3200 BCE and consisted of over 700 distinct symbols that represented sounds and concepts. This sophisticated writing system was used for a variety of purposes, including religious texts, administrative documents, and monumental inscriptions. The discovery of the Rosetta Stone in 1799 proved to be a pivotal moment in understanding hieroglyphs, as it contained the same text inscribed in Greek, Demotic, and hieroglyphs, enabling scholars to decipher this ancient language. This unlocking of hieroglyphic writing was crucial for expanding our knowledge of Ancient Egyptian culture, religion, and history, illuminating the complexities of their governance and societal values through their written records.\n",
              "\n",
              "## 5. Religious Practices\n",
              "Religious beliefs in Ancient Egypt were characterized by polytheism, with a vast pantheon of gods and goddesses attributed to various aspects of life and natural phenomena. Key deities included Ra, the sun god; Osiris, the god of the afterlife; and Isis, the goddess of fertility and motherhood. Temples were constructed as places of worship and to honor these deities, with the Temple of Karnak being one of the most significant, dedicated to Amun-Ra, the king of the gods. The Egyptians believed that maintaining the favor of the gods was vital for harmony and prosperity, leading to elaborate rituals and offerings to appease these divine beings. The religious architecture and practices underscore the central role of faith in guiding the everyday lives of the ancient Egyptians.\n",
              "\n",
              "## 6. Mummification and Afterlife Beliefs\n",
              "Mummification was a vital practice in Ancient Egyptian culture, aimed at preserving bodies for the afterlife. This intricate process involved the removal of internal organs and treatment with natron salts, which facilitated preservation. The belief in an afterlife was central to Egyptian spirituality, with the deceased facing judgment by Osiris, the god of the afterlife. The \"Book of the Dead,\" a collection of spells and incantations, was often included in burial tombs to provide guidance for the soul’s journey through the afterlife. These beliefs not only influenced the practices surrounding death but also reflected the broader cultural focus on immortality and the sanctity of life beyond death, showcasing the ancient Egyptians' complex relationship with mortality.\n",
              "\n",
              "## 7. Social Hierarchy\n",
              "Ancient Egyptian society was structured within a well-defined hierarchy. At the pinnacle was the pharaoh, considered a divine figure with absolute power. Below the pharaoh were nobles and priests, who wielded considerable influence due to their closeness to the divine and their roles in administration. Scribes held an essential position within this structure as the literate elite, responsible for record-keeping and administration. The majority of the population consisted of farmers and laborers, who were crucial for agricultural production along the Nile River. While social mobility was limited, it was possible for individuals, particularly scribes, to elevate their status through education and literacy. This stratified social structure helped maintain order and organization within one of history's most enduring civilizations.\n",
              "\n",
              "## 8. Noteworthy Women Rulers\n",
              "Hatshepsut, who reigned during the New Kingdom (circa 1479-1458 BCE), stands out as one of the most prominent female pharaohs in Ancient Egypt. She adopted male pharaonic titles and often portrayed herself in male attire to assert her authority in a male-dominated society. Hatshepsut's reign was marked by economic prosperity, with successful trade expeditions, particularly to the land of Punt, enhancing Egypt’s wealth. Her monumental building projects, including her magnificent mortuary temple at Deir el-Bahari, showcase her architectural vision and the grandeur of her reign. Hatshepsut's leadership not only challenged gender norms but also solidified her legacy as an influential figure in Egyptian history.\n",
              "\n",
              "## 9. Contributions to Mathematics and Medicine\n",
              "Ancient Egyptians excelled in mathematics and medicine, making significant contributions that laid the groundwork for future advancements. They developed a decimal system for arithmetic and utilized practical geometry for land surveying, particularly important following the annual flooding of the Nile, which reshaped agricultural lands. Medical texts like the Edwin Smith Papyrus provide insights into advanced surgical practices, anatomical knowledge, and treatments for various ailments, reflecting a practical understanding of medicine during their time. This blend of mathematics and medicine highlighted the Egyptians' innovative spirit and their systematic approaches to solving everyday challenges.\n",
              "\n",
              "## 10. End of the Civilization\n",
              "The eventual decline of Ancient Egypt began with foreign rule, starting with the conquests of the Persians in 525 BCE, followed by the campaigns of Alexander the Great in 332 BCE. This led to the establishment of the Ptolemaic Kingdom, which integrated Greek and Egyptian cultures. A key figure during this era is Cleopatra VII, who ruled from 51 to 30 BCE and is renowned for her political acumen and relationships with prominent Roman leaders like Julius Caesar and Mark Antony. Cleopatra’s reign marked the last significant pharaonic rule and culminated in Egypt's annexation by Rome following her defeat by Octavian. This transition from independence to foreign dominance marked a profound shift in the region’s historical trajectory.\n",
              "\n",
              "## Sources\n",
              "- \"The Oxford History of Ancient Egypt\" by Ian Shaw\n",
              "- \"The Complete Gods and Goddesses of Ancient Egypt\" by Richard H. Wilkinson\n",
              "- \"Temples, Tombs, and Hieroglyphs: A Popular History of Ancient Egypt\" by Barbara Watterson\n",
              "- Various academic journals and articles on Egyptology."
            ],
            "text/plain": [
              "<IPython.core.display.Markdown object>"
            ]
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "output_type": "display_data"
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "display(Markdown(report))"
      ]
    }
  ],
